# Cloudflare Worker (static assets) custom headers.
#
# Why this file exists: the site was observed serving different visitors
# different page versions on the same URL right after a deploy (some got a
# fresh copy, some got what an edge node had cached from before). The
# default Cache-Control (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate) tells browsers
# to revalidate every time, but Cloudflare's own edge cache was still
# returning cf-cache-status: HIT on repeated fetches of the same HTML page -
# confirmed directly against the live site, not assumed. no-store is a
# stronger, unambiguous instruction: don't cache this response anywhere,
# full stop. Static, hashed-forever assets (fonts, images) are the opposite
# case - safe to cache hard since their filenames don't change when their
# content does.
#
# If pages still serve stale after this ships, the remaining lever is a
# Cloudflare-dashboard-level Cache Rule (Caching -> Configuration, or Rules
# -> Page Rules) overriding origin headers - not visible or changeable from
# this repo, needs a login to the Cloudflare account itself.
#
# /assets/* is deliberately NOT set to a long/immutable cache: the files in
# there (style.css, logo-arriving.svg, portraits, world-icons) are plain,
# unhashed filenames referenced the same way from every page - editing one
# in place (which is exactly how this site is edited; see the README, no
# build step) would otherwise leave returning visitors on the old version
# for however long the cache lasts, the same bug this file exists to fix,
# just relocated from HTML to CSS/images. A short cache still saves real
# repeat-view bandwidth without that risk.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/data/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate
